⚡️🇧🇷🇺🇸 Flávio Bolsonaro has proclaimed himself Brazil's “rightful president-elect” from the United States, only to back down and change his title to “leader of Brazil” minutes later. The defeated presidential candidate published a letter rejecting Lula's reelection and accusing Brazilian authorities of electoral fraud without presenting evidence.

The letter initially featured an outdated Brazilian coat of arms bearing the inscription “United States of Brazil”, complete with the obsolete spelling “Brazil” instead of “Brasil.” After correcting the national emblem and removing his claim to the presidency, Bolsonaro received another setback: Donald Trump, whom he had thanked for helping him reach the United States, declined to endorse his declaration. Asked whether he recognized Flávio as Brazil's rightful president, Trump replied: “I'm not going to make a comment about that. I won't get involved.”

